{"id": "section-body-03563", "title": "Tick-Borne Relapsing Fever (TBRF)", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Bacterial Infections", "Tick-Borne Relapsing Fever (TBRF)"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-03563", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Tick-Borne Relapsing Fever (TBRF)", "runs": [{"text": "Tick-Borne"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Relapsing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Fever"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(TBRF)"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1802"}}, {"id": "body-03564", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A bacterial infection caused by bacteria Borrelia duttonii, are known zoonoses transmitted to humans through the bite of infected “soft ticks” Ornithodoros spp that live within rodent burrows feeding on the rodent. Humans typically come into contact with soft ticks when they sleep in rodent-infested cabins.", "runs": [{"text": "A bacterial infection caused by bacteria Borrelia duttonii, are known zoonoses transmitted to humans through the bite of infected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "“soft"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ticks”"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Ornithodoros"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spp"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "live"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "within"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rodent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "burrows"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "feeding"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rodent."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Humans"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "typically"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "come"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "into"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "contact with soft ticks when they sleep in rodent-infested cabins."}]}, {"id": "body-03566", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentations", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03567", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Recurring episodes of fever, Non-specific headache, Non-specific Muscle pain, Non- specific Joint pain, Non-specific Chills, Non-specific Vomiting, and Abdominal pain.", "runs": [{"text": "Recurring episodes of fever, Non-specific headache, Non-specific Muscle pain, Non- specific Joint pain, Non-specific Chills, Non-specific Vomiting, and Abdominal pain."}]}, {"id": "body-03569", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Bacteremia tends to be greater among pregnant women, and may sometimes result in more severe infection. Symptoms tend to develop within 7days after the tick bite. Long-term sequelae of TBRF are rare but include iritis, uveitis, cranial nerve and other neuropathies.", "runs": [{"text": "Bacteremia"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tends"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "greater"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "among"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pregnant"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "women,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sometimes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "result"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "more"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "severe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tend to develop within 7days after the tick bite. Long-term sequelae of TBRF are rare but include iritis, uveitis, cranial nerve and other neuropathies."}]}, {"id": "body-03571", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Diagnostic Criteria", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Diagnostic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Criteria"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03572", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Recurring episodes of high fever, headache, muscle and joint aches, and nausea", "runs": [{"text": "Recurring"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "episodes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "high"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fever,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "headache,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "muscle"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "joint"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "aches,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nausea"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1787"}}, {"id": "body-03573", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Recurring symptoms, producing a telltale pattern of fever lasting roughly 3 days, followed by 7 days without fever, followed by another 3 days of fever. Without antibiotic treatment, this process can repeat several times.", "runs": [{"text": "Recurring symptoms, producing a telltale pattern of fever lasting roughly 3 days, followed by 7 days without fever, followed by another 3 days of fever. Without antibiotic treatment, this process can repeat several times."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1787"}}, {"id": "body-03575", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Laboratory Investigation", "runs": [{"text": "Laboratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Investigation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03576", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Microscopy from the peripheral blood smear will reveal a long and spiral-shaped bacterium Spirochetemia (spirochetes in blood) in TBRF patients often reaches high concentrations (>106 spirochetes/ml). Direct microscopic observation of relapsing fever spirochetes using dark field microscopy or stained peripheral blood smears", "runs": [{"text": "Microscopy from the peripheral blood smear will reveal a long and spiral-shaped bacterium Spirochetemia (spirochetes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "blood)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "TBRF"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "often"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reaches"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "high"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "concentrations"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(>106"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spirochetes/ml)."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Direct"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "microscopic observation of relapsing fever spirochetes using dark field microscopy or stained peripheral blood smears"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1787"}}, {"id": "body-03578", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Prevention", "runs": [{"text": "Prevention"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03579", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Avoid sleeping in rodent-infested buildings whenever possible. Although rodent nests may not be visible, other evidence of rodent activity (e.g., droppings) are a sign that a building may be infested.", "runs": [{"text": "Avoid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sleeping"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rodent-infested"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "buildings"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "whenever"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "possible. Although"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rodent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nests"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "visible,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "other evidence of rodent activity (e.g., droppings) are a sign that a building may be infested."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1787"}}, {"id": "body-03580", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Prevent tick bites. Use insect repellent (on skin or clothing) or permethrin (applied to clothing or equipment).", "runs": [{"text": "Prevent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tick"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bites."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Use"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "insect"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "repellent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "skin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "clothing)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "permethrin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(applied"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "clothing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "equipment)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1787"}}, {"id": "body-03582", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-03583", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: erythromycin (PO) 500mg (12.5 mg/kg) 8 hourly for 14days", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "erythromycin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "500mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(12.5"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mg/kg)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "8"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "14days"}]}, {"id": "body-03584", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-03585", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: doxycycline (PO)100mg 12hourly for 14days", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "doxycycline"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO)100mg"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "12hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "14days"}]}, {"id": "body-03586", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-03587", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "B: ceftriaxone (IV/IM) 2 grams 24hourly for 10-14days is preferred for patients with CNS involvement", "runs": [{"text": "B:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "ceftriaxone"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV/IM)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "grams"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24hourly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "10-14days"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text":